      {
        "id": "textbook-function-rules",
        "moduleId": "definition-and-boundary",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "教材：proper function 的三条性质",
        "markdown": "教材把 functional language 中的 proper function 类比为数学函数，并列出三条性质：所有函数都返回一个非 `void` 的结果；结果只依赖输入（arguments）；函数外部的状态不能被修改，也就是没有 side effect。同时满足这三条的函数，才被教材称为 proper function。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-d998d2c477335adeea4bf2f2",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000005"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Types, Objects and Classes",
                "Procedures, Functions, etc"
              ],
              "lineStart": 28,
              "lineEnd": 40,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "1ce5efcea93518f7c1ffbe77a604a153bc81fa8fb2a7463505f601a2fc5ff4ca"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-contrast",
        "moduleId": "definition-and-boundary",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "example",
        "title": "补充对照：一眼区分两类代码",
        "markdown": "可以用一个对照来固定边界：`abs(x)` 对同一个 `x` 永远返回同一个值，也不改变外部状态，因此是 proper function；而 `random()` 没有输入却返回不同结果，`nextCounter()` 每次调用都改写内部计数，二者都不满足“结果只依赖输入”或“不修改外部状态”。判断时依次问两个问题：结果是否只由 arguments 决定？调用后函数外部是否发生了变化？任一答案为否，它就落在 procedure 一侧。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "textbook-function-rules"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "textbook-optimisation",
        "moduleId": "predictability-and-optimisation",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "explanation",
        "title": "教材：standalone 带来的优化空间",
        "markdown": "教材指出，把自己限制在 proper function 之内，可以让 compiler 更容易执行类似 declarative programming 的优化：一个函数完全 standalone，不依赖任何外部状态，于是可以把它单独取出，在无需参考程序其他部分的情况下按需优化。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-d998d2c477335adeea4bf2f2",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000005"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Types, Objects and Classes",
                "Procedures, Functions, etc"
              ],
              "lineStart": 28,
              "lineEnd": 40,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "1ce5efcea93518f7c1ffbe77a604a153bc81fa8fb2a7463505f601a2fc5ff4ca"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-predictability",
        "moduleId": "predictability-and-optimisation",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "explanation",
        "title": "补充：可预测性带来的复用",
        "markdown": "standalone 的直接后果是可预测性：proper function 的行为可以写成一张“输入到输出”的对照表，只要参数相同，无论调用前后执行了什么语句，结果都不变。这也是缓存已经算过的输入输出、以及并行执行能够安全成立的前提：调用顺序与并发都不会改变结果。相反，procedure 的结果依赖调用时的系统状态，这些做法就需要额外的同步或顺序保证。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "textbook-optimisation"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "textbook-side-effect",
        "moduleId": "side-effect-in-code",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "example",
        "title": "教材反例：同一调用得到不同答案",
        "markdown": "教材给出一个反例：数学意义上的函数 `M = L` 总会输出 3，与前后语句无关；但在 Java 中写成 procedure 后，用相同参数连续调用三次会得到三个不同答案。原因在于输出依赖系统中另一份状态 `z`，而调用过程又修改了 `z`，这就是一次 side effect。只给出 procedure 名称和参数，无法预测调用后的系统状态，必须阅读完整定义并分析当前状态。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-d998d2c477335adeea4bf2f2",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000005"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Types, Objects and Classes",
                "Procedures, Functions, etc"
              ],
              "lineStart": 28,
              "lineEnd": 40,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "1ce5efcea93518f7c1ffbe77a604a153bc81fa8fb2a7463505f601a2fc5ff4ca"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-counter-walk",
        "moduleId": "side-effect-in-code",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "worked-example",
        "title": "逐步追踪副作用",
        "markdown": "把上面的反例展开成可以追踪的过程。设外部状态 `z` 初值为 0，procedure 的规则是“先让 `z` 加 1，再返回 `z`”。第一次调用时 `z` 变为 1 并返回 1；第二次调用时 `z` 变为 2 并返回 2；第三次调用时 `z` 变为 3 并返回 3。三次调用的参数完全相同，返回值却不同，差异全部来自被修改的外部状态。若改写成 proper function，例如直接返回参数加 1，那么每次调用都会得到同一结果。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "textbook-side-effect"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "textbook-power-responsibility",
        "moduleId": "tradeoff-and-method",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "note",
        "title": "教材提醒：术语与责任",
        "markdown": "教材给出两点提醒。第一，许多 imperative programmer 把 “function” 当作 “procedure” 的同义词，教材自己也会宽松地使用 “function”，因此听到这个词时需要结合上下文判断。第二，procedure 更强大，但正如 “with great power comes great responsibility”，它给程序引入了一层复杂度：结果可能更好，工作却更难。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
